-- title:
--   Type-ψ primitive classes form at most a line (normal coordinates)
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and $k$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$, let $j_0\colon \mathbb{Z}_{q^2}=W(\mathbb{F}_{q^2})\to k$ be a ring homomorphism, and let $X_0$ be a special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $k$ relative to $j_0$: a commutative two-dimensional formal group law $F$ over $k$ together with an action $a\mapsto \mathrm{act}(a)$ of $\mathbb{Z}_{q^2}$ and an endomorphism $\varpi=\Pi_0$ satisfying the $\mathcal{O}_D$-relations, such that the tangent space splits as the direct sum of the two eigenspaces $\mathrm{lieZero}$ (where $\mathrm{lieAct}(a)$ acts by $j_0(a)$ for all $a$) and $\mathrm{lieOne}$ (where it acts by $j_0(\sigma a)$, $\sigma$ the Frobenius), both invertible modules, and with $\mathrm{act}(q)$ of height $4$. Assume (hsmooth) that the $2\times 2$ linear part of $\Pi_0$ does not annihilate both of these eigenspaces, and (hI) the normal-coordinates condition that the ideal generated by the two components of $\Pi_0$ equals $(X_1, X_0^{q^2})$ in $k[[X_0,X_1]]$. Let $\psi\colon \mathbb{Z}_{q^2}\to k$ be any function (no multiplicativity assumed) and let $g,g'\in k[[X_0,X_1]]$ have zero constant term, be primitive modulo $(\Pi_0(X),\Pi_0(Y))$ — that is, $g(F(X,Y))-g(X)-g(Y)$, and likewise for $g'$, lies in the ideal of $k[[X,Y]]$ generated by the components of $\Pi_0$ in the $X$-variables together with those in the $Y$-variables — and of type $\psi$ modulo $(\Pi_0)$, i.e. $g\circ \mathrm{act}(a)-\psi(a)\,g\in(\Pi_0)$ for every $a\in\mathbb{Z}_{q^2}$, and similarly for $g'$. Then there exist $c,c'\in k$, not both zero, with $c\,g+c'\,g'\in(\Pi_0)$.
--
--   This is the one-variable count in Drinfeld's analysis of special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules: in normal coordinates the quotient $k[[X_0,X_1]]/(\Pi_0)$ is a truncated polynomial ring in one variable, and the classes of primitive series of a fixed type $\psi$ occupy at most a line there. It is the normal-coordinates case from which [`CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormalODModule.exists_smul_add_smul_mem_span_varpi_of_addCoboundary_mem_of_not_and`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormalODModule.exists_smul_add_smul_mem_span_varpi_of_addCoboundary_mem_of_not_and) removes the hypothesis (hI).
